  title: Theosophical Society
  text: Founded in New York in 1875 by Helena Blavatsky and Henry Olcott, the Theosophical Society moved its headquarters to Adyar in Madras. Annie Besant led it, praised Indian culture, founded the Central Hindu College and later the Home Rule League.
